  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adapting to a pandemic: promoting livelihoods for women and young people during Covid-19.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This amendment provides AUGE with 18 months and $158,560 to reach 1,000 additional participants in 55 savings and loan groups, who will create economic resilience through emergency health funds that enable them to pay for unexpected costs without going under. AUGE will also support sustainable agricultural production that improves diet and income for families and will incorporate emotional support and self-help strategies into its organization and its community development programming. As part of the amendment, AUGE is mobilizing an additional $507,580 in counterpart resources to the grant agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
